@startuml donor-first-deployment
title Remote worker on a donor machine, first deployment (revision 4; variants A/B/C, B disabled until separate provisioner spec exists): one invitation, one command, nothing to configure; B has two OS identities; A/C share the donor UID; three role-separated keys stay on the donor; the posture is locked by the donor (the machine's owner)

actor "Donor (the machine's owner)" as ADM
participant "curator remote-worker init\n(donor install)" as C
participant "Separate donor provisioner (B only)\n(binary/schema/rules/removal pending;\nnot swarma-user-manager)" as PH
participant "Bridge role\nB: swarma-bridge-<project> UID\nA/C: donor UID (keys, config, audit)" as B
participant "Harness role\nB: worker-<project> UID\nA/C: donor UID (managed home, scratch)" as U
database "DNS (DNSSEC, default)\nTXT _swarma, TXT _swarma-ssh-ca, TLSA\n(validated inside the client)" as DNS
participant "Join point\n(our host, HTTPS: challenge, cert, collect)" as JP
actor "Operator (our side)\nor orchestrator with onboard grant" as OP
participant "Trust registry + key keeper\n(our host)" as T
participant "swarma-dispatcher (service UID)\nroot swarma-user-manager helper\nproject workplace provisioning" as D

== 1. invitation ==
OP -> ADM: swarma-bridge invitation/1 {invitation_id, join point, root fingerprint,\nSSH host CA fingerprint, TLS pin, declared trust mode, project, role, expires, one-use random code}\nthrough the channel the donor found us by: marketplace deal thread, e-mail, our site\n(the code is a short-lived bootstrap secret; without an invitation: init <domain>, an open application)

== 2. local provisioning (transactional) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker init <invitation-file>\n(file holds the bootstrap secret; no secret in argv)
C -> C: interactive TTY + typed consent + managed-session check (policy heuristic, not proof of humanity);\nrefuse unsupported tuple; verify manifest and variant-owned executable root
alt A (first milestone, no administrator rights)
  C -> C: donor user service, qualified lockdown only; no OS isolation or egress guarantee
else C (no administrator rights, sandbox fallback)
  C -> C: donor user service + qualified sandbox; bridge state excluded; pinned runtime roots read/execute only
else B (one administrator request, future path)
  break provisioner spec/rules/removal or qualification absent
    C --> ADM: B disabled; choose an admitted variant
  end
  C -> PH: provision B-owned accounts/homes/egress/sandbox/system service\n(exact closed operation format pending; no user-manager donor operation)
  alt provisioning succeeds
    PH --> C: journaled result
  else failed or interrupted provisioning
    PH -> PH: undo journaled steps in reverse order; never keep a relaxed rule
    break provisioning failure
      PH --> C: exact failed step; no launch
    end
  end
end
C -> B: three separate keys: K_sig, K_enc (X25519), K_ssh;\nA/C qualified Secure Enclave Macs: P-256 signing/SSH, non-exportable; files elsewhere;\nB: Ed25519 signing/SSH in bridge-owned 0600 files, no Keychain
B -> B: enrolment certificate {K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh, name, role, variant, invitation_id when invited, expires}\nself-signed by K_sig; fingerprint = SHA-256(certificate)
C --> ADM: show fingerprint F

== 3. join (see join-handshake for the transcript) ==
alt invitation declares environment without a DNSSEC domain
  C -> C: select invitation root/host-CA/TLS pins before lookup; Web PKI required
else DNSSEC default (also open-domain applications)
  C -> DNS: TXT _swarma, TXT _swarma-ssh-ca, TLSA; system DNS / DoH transport; local validation
  break mismatch, bogus, failed/malformed read or still indeterminate
    C --> ADM: refused; no invitation fallback on DNS failure
  end
  C -> C: secure records; cross-check invitation pins when present
end
C -> JP: POST /join/challenge (invitation reference or open-application binding; schema pending)\nHTTPS: Web PKI + selected trust pins
JP --> C: enrolment-bound server challenge (5 min, attempt counter)
C -> JP: POST /join/cert {swarma-bridge join/1 transcript, sig_K_sig, code only when invited}\n(HTTPS: Web PKI plus selected DNSSEC/TLSA or declared invitation pins; schemas pending)
alt invited
  JP -> JP: code (constant time), signature, challenge, expiry;\nconsume invitation atomically (tombstone); same-key retry recovers, other key refuses
else open application (no invitation code)
  JP -> JP: signature, challenge, expiry; bounded operator queue\n(binding/retry schema pending)
end
break invalid signature/challenge/expiry, invitation limit, different-key replay or queue cap
  JP --> C: refused; no admission/package
end
JP -> JP: rate limit
JP -> OP: pending enrolment: fingerprint F, name, role
OP -> OP: check the enrolment: the key in the donor's signed marketplace card when there is one,\notherwise invitation binding or open application (no voice check)
alt rejected
  OP -> JP: reject
  JP --> C: refused
else admitted
  OP -> T: pin K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh; root-signed admission "K admitted with role R";\ngrants: post to worker thread, read own mailbox, no delegation, expiry
  OP -> D: provision workplace for K (dispatcher, grant user.create): OS user,\nTrustedUserCAKeys + KRL: short user certificates for K_ssh (principal = workplace user),\nprotected absolute ForceCommand swarma-rb-exec,\nsshd Match: no forwarding, no PTY, no user rc/env; egress by UID
  OP -> OP: swarma-bridge credential-package/1 {root pubkey, operator cert (root-signed), host,\nSSH host CA key, short user certificate/principal, variant, binding digest, qualified tuple, policy generation, expiry}\nAEAD to K_enc (X25519 + HKDF + ChaCha20-Poly1305), AAD = transcript digest, signed by the operator cert
  OP -> JP: package ready for this enrolment (reference schema pending)
  C -> JP: POST /join/challenge (collection phase) -> second server challenge\nPOST /join/collect {enrolment reference, sig_K_sig(second challenge)} (schema pending)
  JP --> C: package
  C -> B: decrypt with K_enc; verify operator cert against the pinned root;\nverify package signature and AAD
  break invalid package signature, chain, AAD, host-CA cross-check, tuple or expiry
    C --> ADM: refused; no activation; package error format pending
  end
  C -> B: write LOCKED machine config: tool_posture=lockdown, permissions=remote-auto (pair),\npolicy_generation, mcp_package_allowlist=[canonical source of swarma-remote-tools],\npassable_env_names=[], qualified tuple, binding, sandbox revision
  C -> U: install the relay declaration into profile remote-worker (absolute command path)
  C --> ADM: registered; waiting for tasks (status, stop, leave, purge available)
end

note over C, JP: Invitation, transcript, package and join API/error schemas PENDING: protocol/remote-worker.md\nOpen-domain init has no code; operator admission and challenge proof remain required.

note over C, T
  Phase: Draft donor target after one-host MVP slice 0; A first, B disabled, C fallback.
  Curator init runs as human donor UID. Bridge-role UID: A/C donor; B bridge account.
  Harness-role UID: A/C donor; B worker account. B provisioner is privileged and separate.
  Bridge role owns three keys, locked config/binding/tuple/generation, audit and cursors;
  harness role owns managed home/scratch. Join point owns challenges, invitation tombstones,
  pending queue and stored packages; registry/keeper owns public pins/admission/grants/CA.
  Project dispatcher service provisions workplace through root account helper;
  workplace UID runs jobs, root owns sshd CA/KRL/forced-command policy.
  Exact join/keeper service UIDs and state filenames unspecified in spec CIP-0009 D4/D9/D12.
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D0-D4/D9/D10/D12]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#publication-status Pending join formats]]
end note

@enduml
